4. Featured DAX Measures

This section documents the most significant measures implemented within the dashboard.

Total Sales

Business Purpose

Calculates total revenue generated from all completed sales transactions.

Dashboard Usage

Executive KPI Card
Trend Analysis
Regional Analysis
Category Analysis

Business Value

Provides the primary revenue metric used to evaluate business performance.

DAX Formula

Total Sales = SUM(Order_Details[Sales])


Total Profit

Business Purpose

Calculates the overall profit generated from sales.

Dashboard Usage

Executive KPI Card

Business Value

Measures the organization's financial performance beyond revenue generation.

Total Profit = SUM(Order_Details[Profit])


Profit Margin

Business Purpose

Measures profitability as a percentage of total sales.

Dashboard Usage

Executive KPI

Business Value

Allows management to evaluate operational efficiency rather than revenue alone.

Profit Margin = 
DIVIDE([Total Profit], [Total Sales])


Sales MTD

Business Purpose

Calculates Month-to-Date sales.

Business Value

Enables executives to monitor current monthly performance.

Sales MTD = 
TOTALMTD(
    [Total Sales],
    'Date Table'[Date]
)


Sales YTD

Business Purpose

Calculates cumulative sales for the current year.

Business Value

Supports annual performance monitoring.

Sales YTD = 
TOTALYTD(
    [Total Sales],
    'Date Table'[Date]
)


Previous Month Sales

Business Purpose

Returns sales from the previous month.

Business Value

Forms the basis for Month-over-Month comparisons.

Previous Month Sales = 
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sales],
    PREVIOUSMONTH('Date Table'[Date])
)

Previous Year Sales

Business Purpose

Returns sales from the previous year.

Business Value

Supports Year-over-Year analysis.

Previous Year Sales = 
CALCULATE(
    [Total Sales],
    SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR('Date Table'[Date])
)
